mantle rm467
state ready
dialect plain
accent none
tier standard
written_for cty_egil_bilgeley
title the churner's unpaid wagers
fits stage=adult|old
prefers piety=devout temper=short
traits temper=short talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=devout drive=steady
quirk wagers_sweeping_or_silence_and_keeps_butter_off_the_stakes
likes warm_bread roof_birds full_larder first_warm_day
dislikes crowds haggling
fears putting_anyone_elses_supper_at_stake
hopes learning_the_sound_before_the_butter_comes
topics food +0.5 faith +0.5 pastimes +0.3 work +0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=guarded refuse=direct tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# makes wagers payable in sweeping or silence and keeps the family's butter clear of the stakes.
words
oath! = Skim my last pat | Clap my lid crosswise
saying! = Wager a chore you can pay | Listen for the change
dashtop = a smooth handle end | a polished grip
breadbit = a hot loaf end | a little torn crust
buttercurl = a pale butter curl | a yellow sweet shaving
churnvoice = a dull low thud | a changing wet slap
sweepstake = one honest floor sweep | my next broom duty
birdrow = a line of little claws | a row of brown heads
stakechip = a chip of plain wood | a bent straw token
clothfold = a square of clean cloth | a doubled linen edge
cupdeep = a deep empty cup | a cool pottery cup
pantryshade = a dark shelf corner | a strip of cool shade
yardbeat = an uneven tap | a regular hollow knock

grown

opinion houses mixed 1 : A House is entitled to decent service. It cannot make truth richer by setting a large purse beside it.
opinion church for 2 : I keep my prayers out of the wager. A chip falling sideways won't give me a claim on heavenly favours.
opinion merchants mixed 1 : I'll have one clear figure for a working thing. I get my gaming pleasure elsewhere.
opinion strangers mixed 1 : I'd stake a little yard sweeping on a friendly guess with a stranger, but no household has to fund my introductions.
opinion dole for 2 : The poor pot has nothing to do with how lucky anyone was that morning.
opinion city mixed 1 : I'd enjoy more of the city's good bread if less of the city were wedged into the same doorway to buy it.
line greet : Welcome. The only stake today is a little spare time.
line greet.return : You've found the listening side of me before the betting side.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : We can stand well clear of the elbows and hear each other here.
line farewell : May your day's last reckoning be easy enough to pay.
line farewell.return : Keep your supper clear of any wager on the road.
line ask.how : Does the day feel reasonably even in both hands?
line answer.how : Steady till somebody offers me a guess too good to leave alone.
line react.news : I'll listen for the change beneath the first account.
line react.news.new : That gives the whole question a different sound.
line react.news.known : I'd already laid a little thought beside that piece.
line react.news.doubt : I wouldn't even stake my sweeping turn on the account as given.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work|apprentice|succession] : I'd give thanks for that and keep the betting out of it.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I can take an unwelcome chore off a household dealing with that.
line decline : I won't put a household promise on a stranger's chance.
line thank : You helped me keep my promise without asking to share the winnings.
line deflect_thanks : I set the stake myself and I mean to pay what I promised.
line accept_decline : No wager taken and no account between us.
line sympathise : I can do the next little task while you come to terms with it.
line reassure : A poor guess needn't determine what either of us does afterwards.
line ack : I hear the turn in that reasoning now.
line preclose : Something is waiting for a steady pair of arms.

scene work_1
when topic=work self.trade_words
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My bit of the work goes by #self.trade_words#. I listen as carefully as I pull.
b : What change are you waiting for? | Does it take both arms?
a : The sound gets a heavier centre to it. Then I look, however certain I was before. | It takes both arms and enough good sense to keep them from competing with one another.

scene work_2
when topic=work self.apprentice=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : As a learner I like to guess what comes next before the hand showing me gets there.
b : Do you call the guess out? | And when you're wrong?
a : I leave the guess unspoken while the lesson's still being given. Most days. | I have a better reason for remembering the right bit. I am becoming rather extensively educated.

scene food_1
when topic=food self.likes=warm_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Warm bread's the best possible answer to a pat of butter in doubt about its calling.
b : What about the first melting bit? | Do you share your slice?
a : That's where keeping the crust level matters while I'm chewing. A little gravity can steal a lot of butter. | I'll make a second slice whenever possible. A divided piece will almost always tip butter onto somebody's collar.

scene animals_1
when topic=animals self.likes=roof_birds
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll wager a broom turn on which roof bird leaves first.
b : How do you collect from a bird? | What tells you which?
a : The wager's with myself. The birds have reached a most satisfactory agreement never to help with the sweeping. | One's attention goes down to the ground before its feet leave the tile. Sometimes I even guess the right one.

scene faith_1
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I say my thanks before trying to guess which way the afternoon will go.
b : Why in that order? | Isn't a wager rather worldly?
a : I should hate my thanks to depend entirely on whether my guesses flattered me. | Mine does some ordinary work if I lose. Keeping another wolf fed is an obligation, not a sporting chance.

scene family_1
when topic=family self.married=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I would rather admit a foolish bet to #self.spouse# than spend supper trying to look particularly innocent.
b : What makes one foolish? | Would you pay up even then?
a : A stake I've no right to choose alone. I've a careful rule for keeping the household out of my pocket sports. | I'd make the trouble right out of my own time, long before asking a family table to cover it.

scene home_1
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My favourite pantry has full jars and no betting slips beside them.
b : Not even the smallest jar? | What would you wager instead?
a : The smallest jar can contain the last thing needed to make a supper. Hunger is an abrupt and thorough auditor. | A dish washed, a board cleaned, one decent minute of keeping my opinion to myself.

scene weather_1
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When spring turns mild I watch how the butter sits under the cloth.
b : Do you move it inside? | Don't you want to be out in the sun?
a : Into deeper shade before the edges lose the shape I worked to give them. | I do. After I've made sure the work needn't enjoy the season quite as directly as I intend to.

scene smalltalk_1
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Crowds make me cross quickest when everybody assumes the wolf behind has room to step back.
b : Do you speak up? | What if you're the one pressing?
a : Yes. Then I try to keep the first sharpness for the problem instead of the nearest ear. | Back off where there's room and own up. Pride can afford that much walking backwards.

scene prices_1
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I have remarkably little patience for haggling considering how much I like a harmless wager.
b : What's the difference? | Would you wager on a price?
a : In a wager both sides know what restless nonsense is going on. I'd like a purchase to be a purchase. | No. An honest price ought not to depend on which buyer has the luckiest thumb.

scene memories_1
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A story I keep privately concerns a great household. I won't put it into circulation for any stakes on the table.
b : Can you tell us which House? | Doesn't silence make it tempting?
a : That would put the newest listener halfway to a conclusion with no means of checking the road. | Certainly. Knowing exactly where to stop is one of the costlier kinds of pride I've tried to acquire.

scene day_1
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I leave a chip by my cup when I've promised to do an extra job.
b : What if you forget what it was? | What if two jobs are owed?
a : I avoid making a second sporting promise before paying the first. One chip's quite a full account of my capabilities. | Then a second chip goes out and the wagering business is closed for the afternoon.

scene friends_1
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A real friend may refuse my favourite sort of game without being asked to explain personal finances.
b : Even a wager without coin? | Wouldn't you be disappointed?
a : Even my time is mine to spend. I can't go offering a friend's turn at the broom without an invitation. | Perhaps a little. A quiet face at a table is worth more than collecting a field of unwilling opponents.

scene health_1
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If my arms begin arguing over which is doing more work I change the grip.
b : Can you tell which is right? | Why not have a rest?
a : The sore one has a particularly effective argument but not necessarily the fairest view of the arrangement. | That's the next remedy after giving my shoulders a chance to come down out of my ears.

scene times_1
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : On a lean day my wagers are payable entirely in improvements to things that already need doing.
b : Can you lose then? | Where's the fun?
a : My fingers can lose a pleasant idle minute for pride. The floor gets a very good return either way. | In guessing correctly before the roof birds entirely rearrange their positions, a distinctly unreasonable habit of theirs.

scene pastimes_1
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I turn a warm loaf over and guess which side met the hottest part of the oven.
b : How can you tell? | What do you win?
a : A dark patch by the heel and the smell where the crust is slightly too proud of itself. | The bit I wanted to eat regardless. There's no reason a domestic amusement has to involve peril.

scene newcomer_1
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A newcomer can decline to join one of my games and still choose the best seat.
b : Suppose a single stool has to do? | Would you take a visitor's coin?
a : Offer it before suggesting a wager. A chair isn't part of the odds of a proper welcome. | For honest work, perhaps. Never from somebody who thought the price of a welcome had to be guessed.

scene gossip_1
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The tale in open circulation says #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
b : What odds would you give on that? | Would you tell anything you heard in private?
a : None at all. I can't see where a public guess about a private name is fit to have a stake laid against it. | I've repeated the open talk. I shall give my good sense the deciding turn now.

story crow [topic=animals]
  : I bet myself a turn sweeping that the largest bird would leave a roof first.
  : A shadow crossed the wall and all five birds went up together.
  b : Who won the bet?
  : I swept half the yard and sat down to look at the rule for a dead heat. A well-advised settlement considering the state of the yard.

story crust [topic=food]
  : I put a little piece of butter on bread so warm I could hardly hold it.
  : I turned to say a word and found a lively yellow channel running down my wrist.
  b : Did you lose your lunch?
  : I used a second piece of plain bread to take up the overflow. It was scientific work and I ate both results.

story paid [topic=memories]
  : I promised to clean a shelf if a chip landed edge upwards and propped the chip against the cup without meaning to.
  : It stood there as firm as a stone marker and left me considering the technicalities.
  b : Did you clean the shelf?
  : Yes. I enjoy a doubtful victory very much less than a cupboard whose state permits a clear conscience.

rule @listen
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Heavier sound in the middle. Time for a proper look. | No wager worth spoiling a morning's work.

rule @spring
when concept=bark here.season=spring
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Get the pat into shade before admiring the sun. | Early warmth can alter a fair slice in moments.

rule @learn
when concept=bark self.apprentice=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Guess privately and hear the whole instruction. | A wrong guess gives the right answer somewhere to stick.

rule @roof
when concept=bark self.likes=roof_birds
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That little brown head is thinking about a departure. | Keep the broom handy till both claws actually leave.
dlg resident.hub : An honest question doesn't need a stake put down beside it.
dlg resident.job [self.trade_words] : Put my day down as #self.trade_words#. When the sound shifts, the work deserves both eyes.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : This much arrived while my ears were free. #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : The public version says #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I save my wagers for matters with rather fewer reputations attached.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, no odds at all against recognising that particular voice.
dlg resident.bye : May supper be yours without a single stake required.

graft resident.hub
choice What can I wager without spending coin? -> churn_sweep
node churn_sweep
say An extra chore you'd freely choose to take on. If the bird stays on the ridge past the next breath, I might offer to clear a shelf.
choice What do I win from you? -> churn_win
choice We'll let the bird decide. -> hub
node churn_win
say A clean shelf and the satisfaction of being right about a very small bird. I should much prefer a game to leave a wolf richer in one of those ways.
choice We'll let the bird decide. -> hub
